// ## 7. Pass-5 — Validator (mcp__blackbox__* tools cross-check)

// Three end-to-end sub-checks against the repo's own tooling. The
// mcp__blackbox__* tools are part of this repo's published surface
// (per `bridge/mcp_server.oo`); validating them on real blackbox
// inputs is the only way to know the tool surface itself is honest.

// | Sub-check | Tool | Input | Result |
// |-----------|------|-------|--------|
// | Autopsy pipeline | `mcp__blackbox__blackbox_autopsy` | `qa/autopsy_null.json` (SIGSEGV, NULL_POINTER_DEREFERENCE at arena.oo:42:5) | **PASS** — returned 1-turn diagnosis: signal=SIGSEGV(11), address=0x0, coordinate=core/alloc/arena.oo:42:5, root cause=NULL_POINTER_DEREFERENCE, RIP/RSP/RBP printed, capability state printed, 1-turn action emitted. |
// | AST diff / token dump | `mcp__blackbox__blackbox_diff` | `record/flight_log.oo` (241 lines, 8 fn definitions) | **PASS** — produced 2061 tokens across 569 lines, clean EOF at `EOF\t569\t1`. Lex+token pipeline functional. |
// | Flight trace | `mcp__blackbox__blackbox_trace` | `.blackbox/flight.json` (1 event, "test trace flight event") | **PASS** — emitted `[1 @ 100ms] INIT::PHASE_CHANGE - test trace flight event`. Telemetry round-trip functional. |

// Validator summary: 3/3 sub-checks PASS. The blackbox tooling surface
// is honest. No findings from the validator pass.

// ## 8. Findings by severity

// **CRITICAL (0):** none in this repo's own surface. The only CRITICAL
// in the org audit (oodac/check/smt/ RFC-0002 evidence gap) is out of
// lane (compiler lane).

// **MAJOR (1):**

//   M1. **Version stamp drift across 4 in-repo sources.** `VERSION` (line 1),
//       `anchor.oo:5` (Setup comment), `anchor.oo:28` (`blackbox_version()`
//       function body), and `AGENT.md:38` (Strict Repository Compliance
//       bullet) all claim `0.0.3`. The ground-truth tag is `v0.0.11`.
//       Drift is +0.0.8. The `blackbox_version()` function is the worst
//       offender: it returns `"0.0.3"` at runtime, so any process that
//       reports its own version via this API is **lying** to its caller.
//       (Plan Q3 considered upgrading this to CRITICAL; the moonshot
//       line 21 claim "v0.0.11 ships" is independently verified by
//       `git describe`, so the shipped version IS v0.0.11 — the
//       inconsistency is a documentation/process bug, not a release
//       blocker. Keeping at MAJOR. Re-evaluate to CRITICAL if a
//       downstream consumer reports a real version-mismatch incident.)
//       Owner: orchestrator lane (this lane). RULES §1.4 (Honesty),
//       §1.21 (Gen semver), §1.24 (Auto-release discipline).

// **MINOR (2):**

//   m1. `cli/cli_run.oo` is at exactly 256 lines (the §1.8 cap, no
//       headroom). Any future addition pushes it over and forces a
//       §1.8 split. The file is also the CLI dispatch router, so it
//       is the natural place to grow. RULES §1.8.
//   m2. `.github/workflows/ci.yml:132-134` downloads `v0.0.10` release
//       binary, but the current tag is `v0.0.11`. Drift is only 1
//       minor version, but the workflow would download a stale binary
//       when invoked with `--target_tag` unset. RULES §1.24
//       (auto-release pin discipline).

// **NOTE (3):**

//   n1. The `AGENT.md` documentation push (commit `14e7ac5`, 70 min
//       before audit) inherited the same stale `0.0.3` claim as the
//       older files. The doc push did not catch the drift. This is a
//       process finding (no version-stamp validator before doc
//       commits), not a code defect. Owner: orchestrator lane.
//   n2. The `qa/` directory has 5 crash JSON fixtures
//       (`autopsy_*.json` for SIGSEGV/SIGBUS/SIGABRT×2/SIGILL) and
//       exactly 1 actual flight record in `.blackbox/flight.json`
//       (1 event: "test trace flight event"). No production telemetry
//       exists; the repo is fresh. The validator pass consumed both.
//   n3. The 4 governance locks (re-derived against blackbox/ alone)
//       all PASS. The moonshot scorecard line 21 claim "blackbox
//       v0.0.11 ships" is also PASS. The only drift is the
//       5-source version stamp mismatch (M1 + m2). The lock and
//       moonshot pipelines are not the source of the drift.

